A||||5||JohnnyK||Oil pan gasket installation questions/problems||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||05-04-2000||07:09 PM||||I have a cork/rubber oil pan gasket made by Mccord (I think, something like that), and I am wondering what the correct procedure is.. In the instructions, it says "If the rear main bearing cap does not have a seal retaining groove, then DO NOT use the rear seal included in this set. Instead, use RTV", Does the Iron Duke have that retaining groove or not? It is a 1985 4cyl SE 5spd... Also, too all who have used this gasket set, what ones go down first, the rubber sides or the cork (Doesn't matter at the front, but at the back, the rubber overlaps the cork, and looks like the cork has to be trimmed?) I'm going to also put a thin layer of RTV over the pan, and then a thin layer over the block... is this an ok idea? I need to figure out that rear gasket seal problem though.. Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||05-04-2000||10:40 PM||||Also, should I use locktite on the bolts?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||05-05-2000||05:38 AM||||I only have experience with the rubber gasket so I'm not sure. I would NOT use locktite on the bolts! There's no gaurentee you'll never have to change the gasket again and getting to the oil pump if needed would be a problem!||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||05-05-2000||03:26 PM||||Also, there is a fairly large (5" diameter approx) round rubber ring.. Where does that go? Can't find it anywhere..<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierospeeder||05-06-2000||02:37 AM||||I have an 84 2.5L fiero and i have done the oil pan two times on it.  <P>I tried the gasket crap, and had it leak after a few months.  <P>A few months ago i just went with ordinary RTV around the oil pan like chilton says to do it.   I had problems with the rubber gaskets leaking on the front and back.<P>Chilton says to use 3/16" wide by 1/8" thick beat the entire oil pan except<BR>the rear part of the pan where its shorter in width, using 3/8" thick bead of rtv<BR>and when you have that groove then it must be filled flush to 1/8" above the surface, which i didn't have on mine||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phaeton||05-06-2000||04:47 AM||||The rear main cap will have a groove cut into it about the same size as the seal, the top of the seal will be barely above the bearing cap and seal against the pan.  It will be obvious if the groove is not there.<BR>The five inch ring should have something to do with the funky in-pan oil filter.||||reg||12
